      "writtenOn": "2026-10-22T06:56:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that\u0027s right. cpi-\u003etd.mb owns the buffers. They\u0027re allocated the first time an IntraBC frame builds the table and freed with the encoder in encoder_alloc.h. The worker threads get thread_data-\u003etd-\u003emb \u003d cpi-\u003etd.mb in ethread.c, so their table is a shallow copy that points to the same buffers. They only read it, and they never allocate or free anything in it. The main thread uses cpi-\u003etd.mb itself.",
      "parentUuid": "b4150329_a1fe671e",
